## battlecode/battlecode26 — the rules, the constants, the maps, the sprites

* Upstream: <https://github.com/battlecode/battlecode26>
* Pinned at tag **`engine.1.2.5`**, commit
  **`991c91af9c35db497f3508393cb6a6f5610725c0`**
* Licence: AGPL-3.0
* Also used at CI time: `org.battlecode:battlecode26-java:1.2.5` from
  <https://releases.battlecode.org/maven> (the same engine, as a jar).

What derives from it:

| here | from there |
| --- | --- |
| `src/battlecode/years/bc26/**` — the ported rule set | `engine/src/main/battlecode/**` (behaviour, hand-ported to Nim; see `docs/RULES.md` for every deliberate divergence) |
| `src/battlecode/years/bc26/constants.nim` | `common/GameConstants.java`, `common/UnitType.java`, `common/TrapType.java`, generated by `tools/gen_year_constants.py` and re-diffed in CI |
| `data/maps/bc26/*.json` | `maps/*.map26`, converted by `tools/convert_maps.py` and re-converted in CI |
| `data/atlas.png`, `data/atlas.json` | `client/src/static/img/**`, cut by `tools/build_sprite_atlas.py` |
| `src/battlecode/years/bc26/chassis/scaffold.nim` | `example-bots/src/main/examplefuncsplayer/RobotPlayer.java`, ported statement for statement (it is the parity oracle's other side, so it may not gain behaviour) |
| `src/battlecode/rng.nim` | `world/IDGenerator.java` plus `java.util.Random`'s documented LCG |

## awu7/battlecode-2026 — the strategy the `awu` chassis distils

* Upstream: <https://github.com/awu7/battlecode-2026>
* Pinned at branch **`final`**, commit
  **`a70328eacaab18622cdac838f5e4e981c2a1f0cd`**
* Licence: AGPL-3.0

What derives from it: `src/battlecode/years/bc26/chassis/awu.nim` and the
modules it calls (`rat.nim`, `king.nim`, `traps.nim`, `dirt.nim`,
`formation.nim`, `targets.nim`, `combat.nim`). **Behaviour, not code** — the
miner/skirmisher split, king spawn thresholding, trap budgets, dirt shells,
formation upgrades and squeak-shared mine locations are its ideas, rewritten
in Nim and parameterised by this coworld's doctrine sheet. None of its Java
is copied, compiled or shipped.

## Everything else

The viewer chrome (`client/chrome_common.js`, `client/broadcast_core.js`,
`client/replay_broadcast.html` and the `replay-viewer/` bundle) is forked from
the `coworld-ctf` starter inside this organisation, and the Nim toolchain and
packages are pinned in `nimby.lock` under their own licences.

The pixel font embedded in `client/replay_broadcast.html` is "NES Pixel" by
Ruilx, built with FontStruct and carried over from that same starter under the
FontStruct licence.
